---
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import ExternalLink from '../components/ExternalLink.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { breadcrumbLd } from '../lib/seo';

const description =
  'Andrew, Michelle, Harrison, Sullivan, and Maeve. A Toronto family writing down the trips and local days they actually take.';
---

<Base
  title="About us"
  description={description}
  jsonLd={[
    breadcrumbLd([
      { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { name: 'About us', href: '/about/' },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="The five of us"
    title="About us"
    dek="We live in Toronto. This is the notebook for the days we leave the house on purpose."
    crumbs={[
      { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { name: 'About us', href: '/about/' },
    ]}
  />
  <div class="wrap stack">
    <section aria-labelledby="family-title">
      <h2 id="family-title">The family</h2>
      <p>
        Andrew and Michelle are the adults. Harrison is nine, Sullivan is six, and Maeve is six, as of 2026.
        That is the whole public roster. It is also everyone who gets a vote on when we stop for snacks.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are a Toronto family. The city is home base: school mornings, a streetcar when the car is the wrong
        idea, and weekends that sometimes stay inside the city and sometimes do not. While We Were There is the
        record of the second kind of time. The outings. The ones worth keeping.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="written-title">
      <h2 id="written-title">What gets written down</h2>
      <p>
        Two sorts of days usually get separated, and they should not. There are the family trips, when we pack
        a bag and sleep somewhere else. There are the day trips, out after breakfast and home before anyone
        has to borrow a pillow. And there are the local days that never leave Toronto at all: a ravine, a
        museum, a neighbourhood we already live beside and still manage not to see.
      </p>
      <p>
        If we went, and we want to remember how it actually was with these particular children at these
        particular ages, it belongs here. A post says where we were, what kind of outing it was, and how old
        Harrison, Sullivan, and Maeve were then. Ages matter. A trail that is a stroll at nine was a carry at
        four, and we do not want to tidy that up later.
      </p>
      <p>
        We would rather publish nothing than invent a place. An empty journal means we have not posted yet. It
        does not mean the week was empty, and it does not mean we are saving a made-up itinerary.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="names-title">
      <h2 id="names-title">Names, schools, and the rest</h2>
      <p>
        First names only. You will not find a surname here, or a school, or a team, or a home address, or a
        routine that would make it easy to find three children who did not ask to be looked up. When we publish
        photographs, they are chosen with that rule already in mind.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you write to us, please leave those details out. A kind note about a park does not need them.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="films-about-title">
      <h2 id="films-about-title">The videos</h2>
      <p>
        The longer films live on YouTube, on the channel <ExternalLink href={site.youtube}>While We Were There</ExternalLink>.
        The writing lives on this site. A story can include one of the films, and the player waits until you
        press play. Some days the video is the whole memory and the page is just the door. The channel is linked
        at the top and bottom of every page for that reason.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="button" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Email Andrew and Michelle</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
